33,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The ferry schedule is a bit tight, and we'd spend two whole days just traveling! Also, last year we barely saw each other during the day. We need to stay together this time!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Two days of travel is exactly what I was afraid of. It's a waste of a holiday. On the other hand, a city trip means we don't have to spend our time staring at a bus timetable.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The offshore houses are priced by the building, which is around 5,400 yen per person per night. However, we need to be careful about how we handle the food costs to keep it fair.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The inn's schedule is way too strict, and sharing one room with everyone on futons sounds like a nightmare. Plus, those island houses have terrible bathrooms. We need a place with actual privacy and flexibility.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Last year's schedule was too fragmented; some of us barely spoke from morning until night. If we want to actually spend time together, we need a structure that naturally keeps us as a group.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, 5,400 yen sounds like a lot! Does that include everything, or will we have to pay for more things later? I don't want any surprise costs!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, don't get worked up over a few thousand yen. The real cost is the time we lose. If we go for the island, we're basically spending a third of the trip just waiting for boats.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, that price is just for the house. Food is extra. I've found that all-in rates can be unfair to light eaters, so paying for meals separately might be more equitable for everyone.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, you're right about the time, but we can't just ignore the living conditions. If we're stuck in one room with no privacy and cold water, the trip will be miserable regardless of how we get there.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, privacy is important, but we should be careful not to overcorrect. If we have too much space or too many separate rooms, we might end up as fragmented as we were last year.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if we pay for meals separately, we won't know the total cost until the end! That's the scariest part. I want a price that tells us exactly what the whole week costs right now!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, your obsession with the total cost is charming, but it's a bit naive. No matter where we go, there will be incidental spending. Let's focus on the logistics; I'm not interested in spending my vacation waiting for a ferry.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, while a fixed price seems safer, it often means some people subsidize others. A system where we pay for what we actually consume is the only way to ensure no one is quietly out of pocket.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Toshio, I'm not talking about having separate houses, just not being crammed into one room on futons. If we don't have a place to just sit and be quiet, we'll all end up annoyed with each other.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"I understand. The key is finding a balance. A town setting provides a natural escape for those who need a moment of solitude, without the isolation that comes from being too fragmented.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I don't care about subsidizing! I just want to know the final number before we go so I don't have to worry about it. Let's pick something with a clear, all-in price!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, your desire for a ""final number"" is a fantasy. Let's be rational: the most expensive part of this trip is the time we waste. A city trip is the only option that doesn't turn into a logistical marathon.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, I agree that efficiency is important, but we must be equally rational about the finances. A clear, all-in price often masks unfair distributions of cost. We need a system that is transparent and equitable for everyone.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, transparency is fine, but it doesn't fix a bad bed or a cold shower. If we prioritize the budget over the actual living conditions, we're just paying to be miserable. We need a place with real rooms.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"It seems we are prioritizing different things: budget, time, and comfort. However, we must remember that the goal is the five of us together. A city environment offers the best balance of accessibility and personal space.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I don't like Option C at all! Separate accommodation means we'll be fragmented again like last year, and we'll never know the total cost until it's too late! I want us to be together!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option C is the only one that doesn't treat our time like a disposable resource. I'm not spending my limited vacation days playing ""wait for the ferry"" or ""wait for the inn's dinner bell.""","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option C is the most problematic for the budget. Separate accommodation and loose plans mean we have no centralized way to track costs, which inevitably leads to some people paying more than others.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option B is out. I can't deal with a strict dinner bell and everyone sleeping in one room on futons. That's a recipe for a disaster. Option C is the only one that gives us actual rooms and flexibility.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option C risks the same fragmentation we saw last year. If we have separate accommodations and loose plans, we are merely five people traveling in the same city, not a group on a trip.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, exactly! We'll just be five strangers in a big city! Option A sounds like a real adventure, and since we're in one house, we can just agree on one big price for everything!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, calling a ferry schedule an ""adventure"" is just a polite way of saying you enjoy wasting hours in a terminal. Option A is a logistical nightmare. Option C is the only rational choice for anyone who actually values their time.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, agreeing on ""one big price"" is exactly what I want to avoid. It creates a situation where the costs are hidden and unfair. Option A's house rental is a fixed cost, but the food would still be a mess.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Rin, Option A isn't an adventure if we're fighting over one bathroom and shivering in cold water. I'm not doing that again. If we want to actually enjoy each other's company, we need a place where we can actually relax.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, I agree that comfort is necessary for relaxation. However, Option A's shared house forces us to move as a unit, which prevents the fragmentation I'm concerned about. Option C is too loose to guarantee we actually bond.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, you get it! If we're in one house, we have to be together! @Asuka, we can just pay for the food all at once at the start! That way, the price is fixed and I can stop worrying!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, paying for food in advance is just guessing, not fixing a price. It's a delusion. Let's be real: Option C is the only one that doesn't involve a logistical slog. I'm not spending my holiday as a passenger.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, paying in advance is just a guess, and it's unfair to those who eat less. It doesn't solve the problem; it just hides it. We need a system where the cost is tied to actual usage.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Toshio, forcing us to move as a unit doesn't work if we're all miserable and sleep-deprived. I'm not sacrificing my sanity for ""bonding."" Option C is the only way to ensure we have a decent place to sleep and wash.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, I understand your point, but Option C is the extreme opposite. If we have separate rooms and separate routes, we risk the same isolation we felt last year. We need a middle ground that balances privacy with presence.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,"I'm voting for Option A! It's a real adventure, we'll actually be together, and we can just decide on a total budget at the start so there are no scary surprises later!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'm voting for Option C. I refuse to spend my precious time off waiting for boats or following a rigid inn schedule. Efficiency is the only way to actually enjoy a holiday.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"I cannot support Option A or C. A is financially opaque, and C is a logistical mess for tracking shared expenses. Option B is the most balanced choice for maintaining a group identity and a manageable budget. I vote for B.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Takumi,,I'm voting for Option C. I can't risk the lack of privacy and the terrible bathrooms in A or the rigid schedules in B. I'd rather be a bit fragmented than be miserable for a week.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"Option A ensures we stay together, but the lack of personal space can be suffocating. Option C is too fragmented. Option B provides a town's natural balance of group time and solitude. I vote for B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
